  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Understanding and mitigating the risks of SARS-CoV-2 transmission from COVID-19 human patients to in-contact farmed and companion animals in the Sultanate of Oman</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is in response to the request of the Sultanate to FAO for assistance in building local capacity in SARS-CoV-2 surveillance in animal species to be prepared and prevent the emergence of future pandemics.


The activities proposed above will involve targeted capacity building activities, in addition to laboratory-based and field studies aiming at assessing the transmission of SARS-CoV-2 from human COVID-19 patients to in-contact farmed and companion animals in select GCC states, and identify key drivers, risk factors and mitigation measures at the animal-human-environmental interface.</narrative>
  </description>
